      "topicId": "math-topic-04",
      "tier": 1,
      "questionText": "Convert the exponential equation $3^x = 81$ into logarithmic form, and find $x$.",
      "options": [
        "log₃(81) = x; x = 4",
        "log₈₁(3) = x; x = 4",
        "log₃(x) = 81; x = 4",
        "log₁₀(81) = x; x = 4"
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "log₃(81) = x; x = 4",
      "solution": {
        "formulaSetup": "Definition of logarithm: $b^y = x \\iff \\log_b(x) = y$, where base $b > 0, b \\ne 1$.",
        "steps": [
          "1. Identify base $b = 3$, exponent $y = x$, and power result $81$.",
          "2. Convert directly to logarithmic form: $$\\log_3(81) = x$$",
          "3. Since $81 = 3^4$, evaluate: $$x = \\log_3(3^4) = 4$$"
        ],
        "finalAnswer": "\\mathbf{\\log_3(81) = x \\implies x = 4}",
        "commonTrap": "Confusing the base and the argument, writing $\\log_{81}(3) = x$."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "m04-q02",
      "topicId": "math-topic-04",
      "tier": 1,
      "questionText": "Simplify into a single logarithmic term: $\\log_2(12) - \\log_2(3)$.",
      "options": [
        "2",
        "log₂(9)",
        "log₂(36)",
        "4"
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "2",
      "solution": {
        "formulaSetup": "Quotient rule for logarithms: $\\log_b(u) - \\log_b(v) = \\log_b\\left(\\frac{u}{v}\\right)$.",
        "steps": [
          "1. Combine into a single quotient: $$\\log_2(12) - \\log_2(3) = \\log_2\\left(\\frac{12}{3}\\right)$$",
          "2. Divide: $$\\log_2(4)$$",
          "3. Since $4 = 2^2$: $$\\log_2(2^2) = 2$$"
        ],
        "finalAnswer": "\\mathbf{2}",
        "commonTrap": "Dividing the logarithms themselves: $\\frac{\\log_2(12)}{\\log_2(3)} \\ne \\log_2(4)$."
      }
    },
    {
