      "topicId": "math-topic-04",
      "tier": 1,
      "questionText": "Solve the equation $3^{2x} = 27^{x-1}$.",
      "options": [
        "x = 3",
        "x = -3",
        "x = 1",
        "x = 1.5"
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "x = 3",
      "solution": {
        "formulaSetup": "Index equation with common base: Express $27$ as $3^3$, then equate exponents.",
        "steps": [
          "1. Replace $27$ with $3^3$: $$3^{2x} = (3^3)^{x - 1}$$",
          "2. Multiply powers: $$3^{2x} = 3^{3(x - 1)} = 3^{3x - 3}$$",
          "3. Equate exponents: $$2x = 3x - 3$$",
          "4. Solve for $x$: $$-x = -3 \\implies x = 3$$"
        ],
        "finalAnswer": "\\mathbf{x = 3}",
        "commonTrap": "Writing $3(x - 1)$ as $3x - 1$ (forgetting to distribute $3$ to $-1$)."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "m04-q07",
      "topicId": "math-topic-04",
      "tier": 2,
      "questionText": "Solve the equation $\\log_2(x) + \\log_2(x - 2) = 3$.",
      "options": [
        "x = 4 only",
        "x = 4 or x = -2",
        "x = -2 only",
        "x = 2 or x = 4"
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "x = 4 only",
      "solution": {
        "formulaSetup": "Product rule: $\\log_b(u) + \\log_b(v) = \\log_b(uv)$ followed by domain check $u > 0, v > 0$.",
        "steps": [
          "1. Combine logarithms: $$\\log_2[x(x - 2)] = 3$$",
          "2. Convert to exponential form: $$x(x - 2) = 2^3 = 8$$",
          "3. Form standard quadratic: $$x^2 - 2x - 8 = 0$$",
          "4. Factorise: $$(x - 4)(x + 2) = 0 \\implies x = 4 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x = -2$$",
          "5. Mandatory domain check: For $x = -2$, original terms $\\log_2(-2)$ and $\\log_2(-4)$ are undefined.",
          "6. Formally reject $x = -2$: Valid solution is $x = 4$ only."
        ],
        "finalAnswer": "\\mathbf{x = 4 \\quad (\\text{reject } x = -2)}",
        "commonTrap": "Failing to reject $x = -2$. Logarithms of negative numbers do not exist in real numbers."
      }
    },
    {
