        "steps": [
          "1. Combine logarithms: $$\\log_2\\left(\\frac{x + 3}{x - 1}\\right) = 2$$",
          "2. Convert to index form: $$\\frac{x + 3}{x - 1} = 2^2 = 4$$",
          "3. Multiply across: $$x + 3 = 4(x - 1) \\implies x + 3 = 4x - 4$$",
          "4. Solve: $$3x = 7 \\implies x = \\frac{7}{3}$$",
          "5. Check domain: $x + 3 = \\frac{16}{3} > 0$ and $x - 1 = \\frac{4}{3} > 0$ (valid $\\checkmark$)."
        ],
        "finalAnswer": "\\mathbf{x = \\frac{7}{3}}",
        "commonTrap": "Multiplying $4(x - 1)$ as $4x - 1$ instead of $4x - 4$."
      }
