        "0.5 ≤ x ≤ 2.5"
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "0.5 < x ≤ 2.5",
      "solution": {
        "formulaSetup": "Base less than 1 inequality: If $0 < b < 1$, then $\\log_b(u) \\ge c \\iff 0 < u \\le b^c$ (inequality flips!).",
        "steps": [
          "1. Domain restriction (strictly positive argument): $$2x - 1 > 0 \\implies x > 0.5$$",
          "2. Convert to index form with sign reversal (since base $0.5 < 1$): $$2x - 1 \\le (0.5)^{-2}$$",
          "3. Evaluate $(0.5)^{-2} = \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{-2} = 4$: $$2x - 1 \\le 4 \\implies 2x \\le 5 \\implies x \\le 2.5$$",
          "4. Combine with domain condition $x > 0.5$: $$0.5 < x \\le 2.5$$"
        ],
        "finalAnswer": "\\mathbf{0.5 < x \\le 2.5}",
        "commonTrap": "Forgetting to flip the inequality sign when the base is less than 1 ($0.5$), and forgetting the strict lower bound $x > 0.5$."
