          "2. From $\\log_y(z) = 3$: $$z = y^3 = (x^2)^3 = x^6$$",
          "3. Note product of base: $$xy = x(x^2) = x^3$$",
          "4. Evaluate $\\log_{xy}(z)$: $$\\log_{x^3}(x^6) = \\frac{\\log_x(x^6)}{\\log_x(x^3)} = \\frac{6}{3} = 2$$"
        ],
        "finalAnswer": "\\mathbf{2}",
        "commonTrap": "Multiplying indices as $2 \\times 3 = 6$ without accounting for the combined base $xy = x^3$."
      }
